":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:fc0160333fec12ac32df94a0bcaf3e8524b6d0ec56b5a2dcb8795d88a2c02a97","file":"preprints/Squared-logarithmic-randomized-k-server-on-arbitrary-metrics-September-24-2026/build/source/latex/sections/01_introduction.tex","line":21,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1603f417a8d57b0ac7f8ad89256743d789629f007be412f89e7da2823e39257c","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Squared-logarithmic-randomized-k-server-on-arbitrary-metrics-September-24-2026/build/source/latex/sections/01_introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:fc0160333fec12ac32df94a0bcaf3e8524b6d0ec56b5a2dcb8795d88a2c02a97","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Squared-logarithmic-randomized-k-server-on-arbitrary-metrics-September-24-2026/build/source/latex/sections/01_introduction.tex#L21"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is an absolute constant \\(C<\\infty\\) such that, for every\ninteger \\(k\\ge2\\), every metric space \\((X,d)\\) with at least \\(k+1\\)\npoints, and every \\(s\\in X^k\\), there exist a randomized online policy\n\\(A\\) and a finite \\(B\\ge0\\) satisfying\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main}\n \\E\\,\\cost_{A,s}(\\sigma)\n \\le C\\bigl(\\log(k+1)\\bigr)^2\\OPT_{X,d,k,s}(\\sigma)+B\n\\end{equation}\nfor every finite request sequence \\(\\sigma\\).\nThe constant \\(C\\) is independent of every property of the metric.\nThe number \\(B\\) may depend on \\((X,d),k,s\\), but not on the sequence\nor its length. The same policy serves all finite sequences and\nhorizons. If the initial positions are distinct, one may take \\(B=0\\)."}
